## THE COMMISSION (RELAYED: gate STATUS B488, read it WHOLE, then the builder's `2026-10-22_B482_STATUS.md`, both in the project's `1_Project_Definition/Briefs/`; if absent, say so, do not hunt)
Gate B488 returned HPSMPOC-178 GO WITH FINDINGS at head `07cd57d2`; PR #187 squash-merged to main at `4e77cf1d` (2026-10-22 13:52:06 UTC = 00:52 AEDT 2026-10-23; Tuesday verified the merge's blobs equal the gated head). The allowance under test: on an update, a stored name that holds a refused character (the C-36 C set) may be sent back UNCHANGED; the comparison is ordinal against the stored name AS SENT, no trim on either side; create never gets it; the length rule is untouched. The gate's three Major findings are test gaps on this correct guard:
- **B488-1 (Major):** the EXACTNESS of the allowance is pinned by no row. Mutants **A1** (`OrdinalIgnoreCase`), **A2** (`name.Trim()` compared) and **A4** (`heldName.Trim()` compared) each leave all 245 rows of the four classes green. Gate's fix-shape: rows sending (1) the held name in another case -> 400, (2) the held name plus one trailing space -> 400, (3) a held name planted with edge spaces, sent back unchanged -> 200 and the stored name is the trimmed text.
- **B488-2 (Major, low blast radius):** mutant **A3** (the whole name block skipped when `name == heldName`) survives, because the existing length row sends a 121-character name that is NOT the held one. On Azure SQL a stored name over 120 cannot exist (`HasMaxLength(120)`, `AssessmentDbContext.cs:137`), so A3 is unreachable in production; on the SQLite test host the row is plantable. Gate's fix-shape: one row planting a held hidden name over 120 characters and sending it back -> 400 `customer.name-length`.
- **B488-3 (Major):** mock mutant **A6** (`b.name.trim() === held`) survives all 149 mock rows. Gate's fix-shape: a mock row sending the held name plus a trailing space -> 400.
- **B488-4 (Note, context for row 3):** the API trims a held name's edge spaces on save (`CustomerEndpoints.cs:198`, `customer.Name = body.Name.Trim()`). Row 3 pins that EXISTING behaviour; it does not change it. A7 (mock, held ignored when `c.name` falsy) is EQUIVALENT per the gate: do not chase it.
Words are the product owner's and unchanged. B488-5 and B488-6 (mock vs API trim at the edge scalars; "as heldIndustry" is not the same trim shape) are Notes: not this round; do not write a row that pins the edge-scalar difference (U+FEFF / U+0085) between mock and API.

