## THE FIX, stated as a property (you pick the exact rows)
**Property P:** *every way the held-name allowance could be widened, namely case, edge white space on either side of the sent name or of the stored name, and length, is refused by at least one row, at the API and in the mock; and the one deliberate narrowing the product has (a held name's edge spaces are trimmed on save) is pinned by a row that reads the stored text.* P is checkable by mutant: each of A1, A2, A3, A4 and A6 (below) must turn at least one NEW row red, and the unmutated main must be green on all rows.
**At least these rows** (names and exact inputs are yours; they follow the gate's fix-shape; use only escapes for any refused character, SYNTHETIC names, 0 non-ASCII bytes added):
- **API row R1 (A1):** plant `HeldName`; send `HeldName` in another case, e.g. `HeldName.ToUpperInvariant()` (the U+202E is unchanged by case mapping; assert in the row that the sent text differs from `HeldName` and equals it under `OrdinalIgnoreCase`, so the row cannot pass by accident) with `staffSize` 420 -> `AssertRefused`; a following `Get` shows the stored name, the facts (null) and the ETag unchanged.
- **API row R2 (A2):** plant `HeldName`; send `HeldName + " "` and, as a second input in the same row or a theory case, `" " + HeldName` -> `AssertRefused` each; stored name, facts and ETag unchanged.
- **API row R3 (A2 and A4):** plant a held hidden name WITH edge spaces, e.g. `"  Probe ‮ Pty (SYNTHETIC)  "` (ASCII spaces only: do not use U+0085, U+000B, U+000C, U+2028, U+2029, U+FEFF, which are the 10 of 636 edge scalars B488-5 measured as differing between mock and API); send it back UNCHANGED with `staffSize` 420 -> **200**, the response `name` equals the planted text trimmed of its edge spaces (assert the expected value is computed from the literal with `.Trim()` and that it differs from the planted text, so the row can tell trimmed from untrimmed), facts saved, ETag changed; a following `Get` holds the trimmed name. State in the row's comment that it pins `CustomerEndpoints.cs:198` as it is (B488-4) and does not endorse it.
- **API row R4 (A4, the independent killer; the drafter's addition to the gate's three, drop it only with a stated reason):** plant the same edge-spaced held name; send the TRIMMED text (`"Probe ‮ Pty (SYNTHETIC)"`) -> `AssertRefused` (the allowance is for the stored value only, by ordinal compare, and the trimmed text is not the stored value); stored name and ETag unchanged. R3 kills A2 and A4 together; R2 kills only A2; R4 kills only A4 (and not A2): so each of A2 and A4 has its own killer.
- **API row R5 (A3):** plant a held hidden name over 120 characters, e.g. `"Probe ‮ Pty " + new string('a', 120)` (assert `.Length > 120` in the row; `Plant`'s own read-back at :255 proves the host stored it, and if the host cannot hold it, say so and STOP: B488 measured that SQLite accepts a 125-unit one); send it back unchanged -> 400 with codes exactly `["customer.name-length"]` (the hidden-character rule is quiet because the name is held; the length rule is not skipped) and the stored name, facts and ETag unchanged. State in the comment that on Azure SQL such a name cannot exist (`HasMaxLength(120)`, `AssessmentDbContext.cs:137`) and the row pins that the length rule is independent of the allowance, not a reachable production case.
- **Mock row M1 (A6):** in `customer-name.test.ts`, `plant(HELD)`; `put(id, etag, { name: HELD + " " })` -> `expectRefused(...)` (400, the ruled error list); the following `read(id)` equals the planted `{ etag, name: HELD }`. Add `" " + HELD` as a second input.
- **Mock rows M2 and M3 (mirror R1 and R3/R4, so the property holds in the mock too; the gate measured the mock exact):** `HELD.toUpperCase()` (assert it differs from `HELD`) -> `expectRefused`; and a held name with edge spaces `"  Probe ‮ Pty (sample)  "`: sent back unchanged -> 200 and the stored name is the trimmed text (the mock stores `b.name.trim()` :92); sent trimmed -> `expectRefused`. Write the mock rows to the mock's own behaviour (the mock's trim is JavaScript's; edge ASCII spaces only).
